<newsitem itemid="27992" id="root" date="1996-09-02" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: JIB Group interim pre-tax profits jump.</title>
<headline>JIB Group interim pre-tax profits jump.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr  (pence)		7.9		    vs 6.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  3.5		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Turnover		    101.9		  vs 93.0</p>
<p> Pretax			16.4		   vs 12.8</p>
<p>NOTE - JIB Group Plc is the holding company of an international group of insurance broking companies and a Lloyd's of London members' agency.  </p>
<p> Operating result	  17.2		   vs 13.7</p>
<p> Investment income	 7.7		    vs 6.4</p>
<p> Interest payable	  0.8		    vs 0.9</p>
<p> Tax			   5.5		    vs 4.1</p>
<p> Net taxed		   10.9		   vs 8.7</p>
<p> Attributable		10.0		   vs 8.1</p>
<p> Pay date		    November 18 1996</p>
<p> Div registration date   October 15 1996</p>
<p>NOTE -- The company expects industry conditions to remain competitive in the next six months, but identified growth potential in the Asia Pacific region.  </p>
<p>NOTE -- Dividend payable as foreign income dividend. JIB expects to recommend an unchanged final full year dividend of 5.0 pence per share if trading continues as expected.</p>
<p>NOTE -- Comparative figures have been restated.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
